@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-content">
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Hear the Call of the Hollow</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title shimmer-text">Hollowbourn</h1>
        <p class="hero-edition">A 2D MMORPG</p>
        <p class="hero-desc">
            Beyond the threshold of Aelunis lies a realm watched by six gods, claimed by three
            rival powers, and haunted by a mystery no scholar has named. Cross over. Learn what
            waits for those marked by the Hollow.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-buttons">
            <span class="btn btn-primary btn-disabled" aria-disabled="true">Download (Coming Soon)</span>
            <a asp-page="/Pantheon" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the Pantheon</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>

<section id="about" class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <p class="section-label">The Premise</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">What Is Hollowbourn?</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
            Hollowbourn is built around the <strong>Hollow-touched</strong>: souls marked in the
            instant they crossed out of Aelunis and into the mortal realm. Where an ordinary life
            would end, theirs does not. Something pulls them into the Hollow instead, a realm
            caught between what is and what comes after, and from there they always return, though
            never without a price. Items and hard-won skill can be lost on the way back.
        </p>
        <p>
            Six gods watch this world, and every school of magic traces back to one of them.
            Three powers (the Crown, the Rival, and the Discord) divide its towns, but their
            rivalry is backdrop, not a side you have to pick.
        </p>
        <ul class="town-list">
            <li class="town-item reveal-up">
                <h3>No Classes</h3>
                <p>A Hollow-touched soul shapes their own path, with no single school or role to be locked into.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="town-item reveal-up">
                <h3>Skills Grow With Use</h3>
                <p>Every skill improves the more you call on it.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="town-item reveal-up">
                <h3>Groups Welcome</h3>
                <p>Travel with others when you want company, go alone when you don't. Never required.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="section-cta">
            <a asp-page="/Pantheon" class="btn btn-secondary">Meet the Pantheon</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
        <p class="section-label">The Realm</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">A Kingdom Divided</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <h3>Calren</h3>
                <p>Seat of the Crown. Proud and ceremonial, it faces the sea as though daring it to approach.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <h3>Grivastel</h3>
                <p>Home of the Rival. Built over crypts, held up by the Rival's coin, and slow to forgive the Crown's taxes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="feature-card reveal-up">
                <h3>Kelgrim</h3>
                <p>Carved from the bones of the Kraghold. The Discord's stronghold, and no friend to the others.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="download" class="section section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner section-narrow">
        <p class="section-label">Join the Adventure</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Download Hollowbourn</h2>
        <div class="ornament-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <p>
            Design docs, engine, and networking are in place; there's no playable build yet.
            Check back here when a client is ready to download.
        </p>
        <div class="section-cta">
            <span class="btn btn-primary btn-disabled" aria-disabled="true">Download (Coming Soon)</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
